==Battleground==
*1 [[Trolly Blogger]] (4,000%) spawns after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Trolly Blogger]] (100%) spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Trolly Blogger]]s (4,000%) spawn, delay 3~12 seconds<sup>90f~360f</sup>.
**20 [[Trolly Blogger]]s (4,000%) spawn, delay 1~3 seconds<sup>30f~90f</sup>.
**40 [[Trolly Blogger]]s (4,000%) spawn, delay 0.67~1 seconds<sup>20f~30f</sup>.
**60 [[Trolly Blogger]]s (4,000%) spawn, delay 0.33~0.67 seconds<sup>10f~20f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Use a [[Manic Macho Legs Cat|Manic Macho Legs]] to kill the first Trolly Blogger with his wave as he dies. Wait for max money and then deploy all the Cats you have. Ranged Cats like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]], Manic Macho Legs, [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Weightlifter Cat]], and [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] are recommended. [[Hermit Cat (Special Cat)|Grandmaster Cat's]] ability to hit the entire battlefield with constant waves while also outranging the Trolley Bloggers makes him an effective choice

A stack of [[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Jiangshi Cats]] can help stop the rush of the Trolly Blogger mob for your heavy damaging units to get a clean shot. Try skipping meatshielding entirely as it will just waste money. With a level 40 Manic Macho Legs and a level 40+ Paris Cat acting as core DPS with whatever other high DPS cats you have you can kill the swarm faster than they spawn, using the money flow from the kills to survive and win.

However, you can still try to meatshield if you really can't beat this stage. A good thing to note is that sending out one level 30 Manic Macho Legs Cat immediately after getting enough cash for it will cancel it out with the Trolly Blogger, allowing you to wait and collect money. Bringing cats with [[:Category:Cats with Knockback Immunity|Knockback Immunity]] will make this stage less stressful and annoying, but isn't necessary. Considering the Trolly Blogger's short range and relatively low health even under extreme buffs, a sufficiently large stack of attackers will plow through them anyway.

